================================================================================
## Track simulation runs in Background Tasks
================================================================================

Context: A what-if run created a TaskManager job but the navbar hourglass
did not pick it up immediately, so users could not follow progress after
leaving the workbench.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/simulation/js/simulation.js
   Refresh the navbar task list when a run starts, finishes, or fails.
2. src/front/static/global/js/task-tracker.js
   Map simulation tasks to the workbench and open the scenario from the
   hourglass row.
3. src/back/objects/simulation/Simulation.py
   Publish simulation_id on the running task so the tracker can deep-link.
4. src/front/static/simulation/js/simulation-workbench.js
   Load ?simulation= into the editor.
5. docs/user-guide.md and help_modal.html
   Document following a run from Background Tasks.

